# Controllers

Follow `users.controller.ts` / `profile.controller.ts`.

```typescript
@Post()
@UseGuards(AuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles([UserRole.ADMIN])
@Serialize(UserResponseDto)
@ResponseMessage(ApiMessage.USER_CREATED)
create(@Body() dto: CreateUserDto) {
  return this.usersService.create(dto);
}
```

## Rules

- Thin handlers: one service call
- Guard order: `AuthGuard` then `RolesGuard`
- Admin catalog writes: `@Roles([UserRole.ADMIN])`
- Public storefront reads: unguarded only when intentional (e.g. categories GET)
- Self-service: class-level `@UseGuards(AuthGuard)` + `@CurrentUser()` (profile)
- Always pair `@Serialize` + `@ResponseMessage` on handlers that return entities
- Pass Mongo `:id` as `string` — never `+id`
- `@Controller` path must be **plural** for CRUD resources (`categories`, not `category`)

## Auth surfaces

| Area | Auth |
|------|------|
| `auth/*` | Public |
| `profile/*` | JWT |
| `users/*` writes/lists | JWT + roles as on controller |
| `categories` POST/PATCH/DELETE | JWT + ADMIN |
| `categories` GET | Public |
